<title>RUSSIA: Russian LUKoil to boost capex in 1997.</title>
<headline>Russian LUKoil to boost capex in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's NK LUKoil plans to boost capital expenditure by 25 percent this year to 7.7 trillion roubles, a company spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said LUKoil, Russia's largest oil producer, would use 80 percent of the figure for investment in crude oil production.</p>
<p>He also repeated LUKoil statements that the firm would raise capital abroad, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>LUKoil's capital expenditure last year totalled 6.2 trillion roubles, of which 1.5 trillion roubles came from debts, share issues and other financial instruments.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($1 = 5,625 roubles)</p>
